            <div xml:id="d323">

                <pb facs="0406" n="294" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg294"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/6700: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Commission to Negotiate Peace to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-08-07T15:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">August 7, 1919,
                                3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 4:14 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>3546. For the Secretary of State from Polk.</p>
                <p>A communication from French Embassy, Washington, presented to Conference
                    yesterday stated that United States could not assist in repatriation of Czechs
                    owing to lack of shipping and suggested that they go out in the direction of
                    General Denikine’s forces. Allied military authorities say suggestion out of the
                    question. Would it not be possible to do something, as I understand we are to be
                    reimbursed for any expense and it would seem that we were under an obligation to
                    do everything in our power.</p>
                <closer><hi rendition="#small-caps">American Mission</hi></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
